Boudewijn Waijers wrote:

> Why? You should always keep at least one wish in reserve, I think.
> 

The problem with keeping a wish in reserve is that it's never guaranteed 
to be available when you need it. Magic lamps often don't work on the 
first try, and if you're getting the last charge out of the wand, it 
takes a while. In most situations when you'd be glad you had a wish in 
reserve, time is essential and you can't afford to spend several turns 
getting the wish.

I've found it's better to use the wish early, and be well enough 
prepared to not NEED the wish later.

